Rust is installed now. Great!

To get started you need Cargo's bin directory 
(/tmp/crosslang-toolchains/cargo-home/bin) in your PATH
environment variable. This has not been done automatically.

To configure your current shell, you need to source
the corresponding env file under /tmp/crosslang-toolchains/cargo-home.

This is usually done by running one of the following (note the leading DOT):
. "/tmp/crosslang-toolchains/cargo-home/env"            # For 
sh/bash/zsh/ash/dash/pdksh
source "/tmp/crosslang-toolchains/cargo-home/env.fish"  # For fish
source "/tmp/crosslang-toolchains/cargo-home/env.nu"  # For nushell
source "/tmp/crosslang-toolchains/cargo-home/env.tcsh"  # For tcsh
. "/tmp/crosslang-toolchains/cargo-home/env.ps1"        # For pwsh
source "/tmp/crosslang-toolchains/cargo-home/env.xsh"   # For xonsh
